sed. [Data: Entities (3201, 5115)]\\n\\nA separate relationship connects PAPILLARY TUMOR to the TRACHEA, describing that a tumor near or abutting the trachea is in a high-risk location that affects suitability for active surveillance. This introduces an anatomical risk criterion that can limit surveillance eligibility, emphasizing that ‘low risk’ depends not only on tumor type/size but also on location. [Data: Relationships (11267); Entities (5115)]\"}],\"rating\":3.2,\"rating_explanation\":\"Impact is assessed as low-to-moderate because the community describes standard clinical management and monitoring pathways (active surveillance, testing, treatment options) without allegations of wrongdoing or atypical high-risk capabilities.\"}", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "stop"}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1186, "prompt_tokens": 2777, "total_tokens": 3963, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null, "text_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1536, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}}, "service_tier": null}}}